  "contentHtml": "<p data-start=\"744\" data-end=\"983\">Understanding <strong data-start=\"758\" data-end=\"798\">how to calculate leave salary in UAE</strong> is essential for every employee and HR professional. The updated <a href=\"/labor-law-in-uae/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UAE Labor Law</a> ensures that all workers, whether full-time or part-time are entitled to fair <strong data-start=\"959\" data-end=\"980\">paid annual leave</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"985\" data-end=\"1321\">Knowing the exact calculation method helps you manage your finances, plan time off responsibly, and confirm that your employer is following legal standards. In this guide, we’ll break down every detail from eligibility to step-by-step calculation with 2026 updates under the <strong data-start=\"1264\" data-end=\"1318\">UAE Labour Law (<a href=\"https://uaelegislation.gov.ae/en/legislations/1541/download\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021</a>)</strong>.</p>\n<blockquote data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1538\">\n<p data-start=\"1325\" data-end=\"1538\"><strong data-start=\"1328\" data-end=\"1345\">Did you know?</strong> According to MOHRE data (2024), 78% of private-sector employees in the UAE use their annual leave benefits each year but less than half know how their leave salary is calculated correctly.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 24px;\" id=\"what-is-leave-salary-in-the-uae\">What Is Leave Salary in the UAE?</h2>\n<p data-start=\"1588\" data-end=\"1794\"><strong data-start=\"1588\" data-end=\"1604\">Leave salary</strong> refers to the <strong data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1682\">amount paid to an employee during their annual leave period</strong>, based on their basic salary. It ensures that employees can enjoy their vacations without financial concerns.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1822\">Under the UAE labor law:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1823\" data-end=\"2058\">\n<li data-start=\"1823\" data-end=\"1932\">\n<p data-start=\"1825\" data-end=\"1932\">Employees who complete <strong data-start=\"1848\" data-end=\"1871\">one year of service</strong> are entitled to <strong data-start=\"1888\" data-end=\"1929\">30 calendar days of paid annual leave</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1933\" data-end=\"2058\">\n<p data-start=\"1935\" data-end=\"2058\">Those who have worked <strong data-start=\"1957\" data-end=\"2002\">more than six months but less than a year</strong> are entitled to <strong data-start=\"2019\" data-end=\"2055\">two days of paid leave per month</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"2060\" data-end=\"2221\">For more information, you can visit the <strong data-start=\"2100\" data-end=\"2154\"><a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"https://www.mohre.gov.ae\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"2102\" data-end=\"2152\">MOHRE official website</a></strong> — which governs all employment and labor regulations in the UAE.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 20px;\" id=\"eligibility-for-paid-leave-in-the-uae\">Eligibility for Paid Leave in the UAE:</h3>\n<p data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2439\">Every employee working under a valid UAE employment contract is entitled to paid leave, provided they’ve completed the minimum service period.</p>\n<p data-start=\"2441\" data-end=\"2466\">Key eligibility points:</p>\n<ol data-start=\"2467\" data-end=\"2948\">\n<li data-start=\"2467\" data-end=\"2564\">\n<p data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2564\"><strong data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2494\">Full-time Employees:</strong> Entitled to 30 calendar days after 12 months of continuous service.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2565\" data-end=\"2670\">\n<p data-start=\"2568\" data-end=\"2670\"><strong data-start=\"2568\" data-end=\"2589\">Probation Period:</strong> Leave accrues during probation but cannot be availed until after confirmation.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2671\" data-end=\"2744\">\n<p data-start=\"2674\" data-end=\"2744\"><strong data-start=\"2674\" data-end=\"2691\">Unpaid Leave:</strong> Any unpaid days are excluded from the calculation.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2745\" data-end=\"2843\">\n<p data-start=\"2748\" data-end=\"2843\"><strong data-start=\"2748\" data-end=\"2772\">Part-time Employees:</strong> Receive leave salary on a <strong data-start=\"2799\" data-end=\"2817\">pro-rata basis</strong> based on working hours.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"2948\">\n<p data-start=\"2847\" data-end=\"2948\"><strong data-start=\"2847\" data-end=\"2871\">Carry Forward Leave:</strong> With mutual agreement, unused leave can be carried forward or compensated.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<blockquote data-start=\"2950\" data-end=\"3058\">\n<p data-start=\"2952\" data-end=\"3058\"><em data-start=\"2954\" data-end=\"2960\">Tip:</em> Always maintain a record of your accrued and used leave days through your HR portal or payslip.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p data-start=\"2952\" data-end=\"3058\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-74521 \" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Understanding-UAE-Leave-Salary.png\" alt=\"how to calculate leave salary in uae\" width=\"601\" height=\"433\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Understanding-UAE-Leave-Salary.png 805w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Understanding-UAE-Leave-Salary-300x216.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Understanding-UAE-Leave-Salary-150x108.png 150w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Understanding-UAE-Leave-Salary-20x14.png 20w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Understanding-UAE-Leave-Salary-555x400.png 555w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 601px) 100vw, 601px\"></p>\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 24px;\" id=\"how-to-calculate-leave-salary-in-uae\">How to Calculate Leave Salary in UAE?</h2>\n<p data-start=\"3131\" data-end=\"3212\">The <strong data-start=\"3135\" data-end=\"3159\">leave salary formula</strong> is simple and defined clearly under UAE labor law:</p>\n<p data-start=\"3214\" data-end=\"3285\"><strong data-start=\"3214\" data-end=\"3283\">Leave Salary = (Basic Monthly Salary ÷ 30) × Number of Leave Days</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"3287\" data-end=\"3325\">Let’s break it down with an example:</p>\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"3327\" data-end=\"3618\">\n<thead data-start=\"3327\" data-end=\"3413\">\n<tr data-start=\"3327\" data-end=\"3413\">\n<th data-start=\"3327\" data-end=\"3338\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Employee</th>\n<th data-start=\"3338\" data-end=\"3359\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Basic Salary (AED)</th>\n<th data-start=\"3359\" data-end=\"3372\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Leave Days</th>\n<th data-start=\"3372\" data-end=\"3391\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Daily Rate (AED)</th>\n<th data-start=\"3391\" data-end=\"3413\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Leave Salary (AED)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody data-start=\"3500\" data-end=\"3618\">\n<tr data-start=\"3500\" data-end=\"3538\">\n<td data-start=\"3500\" data-end=\"3504\" data-col-size=\"sm\">A</td>\n<td data-start=\"3504\" data-end=\"3512\" data-col-size=\"sm\">7,000</td>\n<td data-start=\"3512\" data-end=\"3517\" data-col-size=\"sm\">15</td>\n<td data-start=\"3517\" data-end=\"3526\" data-col-size=\"sm\">233.33</td>\n<td data-start=\"3526\" data-end=\"3538\" data-col-size=\"sm\">3,499.95</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"3539\" data-end=\"3578\">\n<td data-start=\"3539\" data-end=\"3543\" data-col-size=\"sm\">B</td>\n<td data-start=\"3543\" data-end=\"3552\" data-col-size=\"sm\">10,000</td>\n<td data-start=\"3552\" data-end=\"3557\" data-col-size=\"sm\">30</td>\n<td data-start=\"3557\" data-end=\"3566\" data-col-size=\"sm\">333.33</td>\n<td data-start=\"3566\" data-end=\"3578\" data-col-size=\"sm\">9,999.90</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"3579\" data-end=\"3618\">\n<td data-start=\"3579\" data-end=\"3583\" data-col-size=\"sm\">C</td>\n<td data-start=\"3583\" data-end=\"3592\" data-col-size=\"sm\">12,000</td>\n<td data-start=\"3592\" data-end=\"3597\" data-col-size=\"sm\">10</td>\n<td data-start=\"3597\" data-end=\"3606\" data-col-size=\"sm\">400.00</td>\n<td data-start=\"3606\" data-end=\"3618\" data-col-size=\"sm\">4,000.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p data-start=\"3620\" data-end=\"3650\"><strong data-start=\"3623\" data-end=\"3648\">Step-by-Step Example:</strong></p>\n<ol data-start=\"3651\" data-end=\"3819\">\n<li data-start=\"3651\" data-end=\"3714\">\n<p data-start=\"3654\" data-end=\"3714\"><strong data-start=\"3654\" data-end=\"3688\">Find your basic monthly salary</strong> (excluding allowances).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3715\" data-end=\"3760\">\n<p data-start=\"3718\" data-end=\"3760\"><strong data-start=\"3718\" data-end=\"3734\">Divide by 30</strong> to get your daily rate.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3761\" data-end=\"3819\">\n<p data-start=\"3764\" data-end=\"3819\"><strong data-start=\"3764\" data-end=\"3776\">Multiply</strong> the daily rate by your total leave days.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-start=\"3821\" data-end=\"3920\">That’s your <strong data-start=\"3833\" data-end=\"3855\">total leave salary</strong>, which must be <strong data-start=\"3871\" data-end=\"3896\">paid before the start</strong> of your annual leave.</p>\n<blockquote data-start=\"3922\" data-end=\"4062\">\n<p data-start=\"3924\" data-end=\"4062\"><strong data-start=\"3927\" data-end=\"3942\">Legal Note:</strong> According to <strong data-start=\"3956\" data-end=\"3988\">Article 29 of UAE Labour Law</strong>, employers must pay leave salary before the employee proceeds on leave.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p data-start=\"3924\" data-end=\"4062\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-74522 aligncenter\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Calculating-Leave-Salary-in-UAE.png\" alt=\"Calculating Leave Salary in UAE\" width=\"550\" height=\"424\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Calculating-Leave-Salary-in-UAE.png 591w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Calculating-Leave-Salary-in-UAE-300x231.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Calculating-Leave-Salary-in-UAE-150x116.png 150w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Calculating-Leave-Salary-in-UAE-20x15.png 20w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Calculating-Leave-Salary-in-UAE-518x400.png 518w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 550px) 100vw, 550px\"></p>\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 24px;\" id=\"what-happens-to-leave-salary-during-final-settlement\">What Happens to Leave Salary During Final Settlement?</h2>\n<p data-start=\"4152\" data-end=\"4275\">If you resign or your contract ends, <strong data-start=\"4189\" data-end=\"4205\">unused leave</strong> will be converted into cash and added to your <strong data-start=\"4252\" data-end=\"4272\">final settlement</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"4277\" data-end=\"4358\">Formula remains the same:<br data-start=\"4302\" data-end=\"4305\"><strong data-start=\"4305\" data-end=\"4356\">(Basic Monthly Salary ÷ 30) × Unused Leave Days</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"4360\" data-end=\"4466\">For instance, if you earn AED 9,000 and have 10 unused leave days, your employer owes you <strong data-start=\"4450\" data-end=\"4463\">AED 3,000</strong>.</p>\n<blockquote data-start=\"4468\" data-end=\"4628\">\n<p data-start=\"4470\" data-end=\"4628\"><em data-start=\"4473\" data-end=\"4500\">Tip from PEO Middle East:</em> Always cross-check your final settlement sheet before signing to ensure that unused leave compensation is correctly included.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 20px;\" id=\"emergency-leave-and-leave-salary\">Emergency Leave and Leave Salary:</h3>\n<p data-start=\"4697\" data-end=\"4903\">Emergency leaves are separate from annual leaves but may be <strong data-start=\"4757\" data-end=\"4775\">paid or unpaid</strong> depending on company policy. However, <strong data-start=\"4814\" data-end=\"4877\">the calculation method for paid emergency leave is the same</strong> as annual leave salary.</p>\n<blockquote data-start=\"4905\" data-end=\"5023\">\n<p data-start=\"4907\" data-end=\"5023\"><em data-start=\"4910\" data-end=\"4942\">Check your company’s HR policy</em> — some employers allow converting unpaid emergency leave into paid days later.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p data-start=\"4907\" data-end=\"5023\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-74523 aligncenter\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/What-happens-to-unused-leave-during-final-settlement.png\" alt=\"What happens to unused leave during final settlement\" width=\"550\" height=\"411\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/What-happens-to-unused-leave-during-final-settlement.png 646w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/What-happens-to-unused-leave-during-final-settlement-300x224.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/What-happens-to-unused-leave-during-final-settlement-150x112.png 150w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/What-happens-to-unused-leave-during-final-settlement-20x15.png 20w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/What-happens-to-unused-leave-during-final-settlement-535x400.png 535w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 550px) 100vw, 550px\"></p>\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 24px;\" id=\"uae-specific-considerations\">UAE-Specific Considerations:</h2>\n<p data-start=\"5087\" data-end=\"5234\">When calculating leave salary, HR teams must comply with the <strong data-start=\"5148\" data-end=\"5184\">UAE Wage Protection System (WPS)</strong> and local data privacy rules.<br data-start=\"5214\" data-end=\"5217\">Employers must:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"5235\" data-end=\"5376\">\n<li data-start=\"5235\" data-end=\"5292\">\n<p data-start=\"5237\" data-end=\"5292\">Pay leave salary through <strong data-start=\"5262\" data-end=\"5289\">registered WPS channels</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5293\" data-end=\"5341\">\n<p data-start=\"5295\" data-end=\"5341\">Maintain accurate records of leave balances.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5342\" data-end=\"5376\">\n<p data-start=\"5344\" data-end=\"5376\">Avoid any unlawful deductions.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"5378\" data-end=\"5476\">Additionally, <strong data-start=\"5392\" data-end=\"5411\">public holidays</strong> during annual leave are <strong data-start=\"5436\" data-end=\"5451\">not counted</strong> as part of leave days.</p>\n<blockquote data-start=\"5478\" data-end=\"5662\">\n<p data-start=\"5480\" data-end=\"5662\">For compliance support, visit <a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" href=\"/hr-consultancy-uae/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"5513\" data-end=\"5603\">PEO Middle East’s HR and Payroll Services</a> to automate your payroll and leave management processes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 24px;\" id=\"why-accurate-leave-salary-calculation-matters\">Why Accurate Leave Salary Calculation Matters:</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"5744\" data-end=\"5939\">\n<li data-start=\"5744\" data-end=\"5788\">\n<p data-start=\"5746\" data-end=\"5788\">Builds <strong data-start=\"5753\" data-end=\"5785\">employee trust and retention</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5789\" data-end=\"5842\">\n<p data-start=\"5791\" data-end=\"5842\">Prevents <strong data-start=\"5800\" data-end=\"5818\">legal disputes</strong> under UAE labor laws.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5843\" data-end=\"5892\">\n<p data-start=\"5845\" data-end=\"5892\">Improves <strong data-start=\"5854\" data-end=\"5874\">payroll accuracy</strong> and compliance.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5893\" data-end=\"5939\">\n<p data-start=\"5895\" data-end=\"5939\">Reflects professionalism in HR operations.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote data-start=\"5941\" data-end=\"6088\">\n<p data-start=\"5943\" data-end=\"6088\">A 2024 HR survey revealed that <strong data-start=\"5977\" data-end=\"6053\">companies using automated payroll systems reduced salary disputes by 40%</strong> compared to manual calculations.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 style=\"font-size: 20px;\" id=\"pro-tips-for-employees\">Pro Tips for Employees:</h3>\n<ol data-start=\"6147\" data-end=\"6460\">\n<li data-start=\"6147\" data-end=\"6211\">\n<p data-start=\"6150\" data-end=\"6211\">Always <strong data-start=\"6157\" data-end=\"6192\">review your employment contract</strong> for leave terms.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6212\" data-end=\"6264\">\n<p data-start=\"6215\" data-end=\"6264\">Keep a <strong data-start=\"6222\" data-end=\"6250\">record of leave balances</strong> in writing.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6265\" data-end=\"6328\">\n<p data-start=\"6268\" data-end=\"6328\">Request your <strong data-start=\"6281\" data-end=\"6302\">leave salary slip</strong> before taking time off.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6329\" data-end=\"6376\">\n<p data-start=\"6332\" data-end=\"6376\">Discuss discrepancies with HR immediately.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6377\" data-end=\"6460\">\n<p data-start=\"6380\" data-end=\"6460\">Refer to <a href=\"https://backoffice.mohre.gov.ae/mohre.complaints.app/TwafouqAnonymous2/CallerVerification?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong data-start=\"6389\" data-end=\"6426\">MOHRE’s employee grievance portal</strong></a> if your leave salary is unpaid.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-74524 aligncenter\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ensuring-Accurate-Leave-Salary.png\" alt=\"Ensuring Accurate Leave Salary\" width=\"646\" height=\"270\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ensuring-Accurate-Leave-Salary.png 933w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ensuring-Accurate-Leave-Salary-300x125.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ensuring-Accurate-Leave-Salary-150x63.png 150w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ensuring-Accurate-Leave-Salary-20x8.png 20w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ensuring-Accurate-Leave-Salary-600x251.png 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 646px) 100vw, 646px\"></p>\n<p data-start=\"6769\" data-end=\"6839\">\n</p><h2 style=\"font-size: 24px;\" id=\"final-thoughts\">Final Thoughts:</h2>\n<p data-start=\"6870\" data-end=\"7098\">Understanding <strong data-start=\"6884\" data-end=\"6924\">how to calculate leave salary in UAE</strong> gives employees confidence and employers clarity. Whether you’re planning your annual vacation or preparing a final settlement, accuracy is key to compliance and fairness.</p>\n<p data-start=\"7100\" data-end=\"7330\">At <a href=\"/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong data-start=\"7103\" data-end=\"7122\">PEO Middle East</strong></a>, we specialize in <strong data-start=\"7141\" data-end=\"7203\"><a href=\"/hr-consultancy-uae/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HR outsourcing</a>, <a href=\"/uae-payroll-outsourcing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">payroll management</a>, and compliance support</strong> across the UAE and GCC. Our team ensures your business meets legal standards while keeping employees satisfied and informed.</p>\n<p data-start=\"7334\" data-end=\"7499\">📞 <strong data-start=\"7337\" data-end=\"7359\">Get in touch today</strong> to streamline your payroll and HR compliance across the Middle East.<br data-start=\"7428\" data-end=\"7431\">👉 <a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" href=\"/request-a-quote/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"7434\" data-end=\"7497\">Contact PEO Middle East</a></p>\n",
